    socialLife: 'Dubai\'s social scene is relentlessly busy and brilliantly international — brunches are a weekly institution, rooftop bars are world-class, and the nightlife rivals London and New York. Abu Dhabi is quieter but has excellent cultural institutions (Louvre Abu Dhabi, upcoming Guggenheim). Alcohol is served in licensed venues (hotels, specific restaurants) — no longer requires a personal licence as of 2023. Ramadan transforms the social calendar (daytime eating/drinking is restricted publicly). The UAE is generally socially conservative in public — PDA and immodest dress in non-resort areas is inappropriate. Dubai has a strong LGBTQ+ expat presence though same-sex relationships are technically illegal.',
